condition_name: Glaucoma
condition_slug: glaucoma
source: NSTG 2022
introduction: "The glaucomas are a group of diseases in which there is gradual loss of vision (actually visual field) due to a form of optic neuropathy. A raised intraocular pressure is a risk factor. It is a common cause of blindness worldwide and once a patient is blind from glaucoma, vision cannot be restored."
clinical_features[3]:
  - type: primary open angle glaucoma
    features[1]: generally symptomless except in the late stages when symptoms of visual loss present
  - type: congenital glaucoma
    features[3]: enlarged eyeball(s) in the newborn,corneal oedema/opacity,photophobia and watering
  - type: acute closed angle glaucoma
    features[4]: marked elevation of intraocular pressure with severe pain,"reduction in vision, red eye",fixed mid-dilated pupil,shallow anterior chamber
investigations[4]: Intraocular pressure measurement,Central and peripheral visual field test.,Fundoscopy to determine cup/disc ratio,Gonioscopy to view the angle of the eye
treatment:
  goals[1]: Stop further loss of retinal ganglion cells and nerve fibre layer by prompt treatment.
  non_drug[0]:
  drug[6]: Beta-blockers e.g. timolol,Parasympathomimetics e.g. pilocarpine,"Sympathomimetics e.g. adrenaline, dipivefrin","Carbonic anhydrase inhibitors e.g. acetazolamide, dorzolamide",Prostaglandin analogues e.g. latanoprost,"Hyperosmotic agents e.g. mannitol, glycerol"
  adverse_reactions_and_cautions[7]: "Timolol - can precipitate heart block, bradycardia and bronchospasms","Pilocarpine - mioses, spasms of accommodation, retinal detachment","Acetazolamide - paraesthesia, renal stone formation, Steven – Johnson syndrome, gastrointestinal disturbances, decreased libido, fatigue, weight loss.","Latanoprost –foreign body sensation, mild conjunctival hyperaemia and increased pigmentation of iris",Timoptol is contraindicated in Asthmatics and patients with heart block.,"Acetazolamide is contraindicated in patients with pre-existing systemic acidosis, patients with sickle cell disease and allergy to sulphonamides.","Pilocarpine is contraindicated in eyes with previous retinal detachment, and pathological myopia."
  supportive_measures[0]:
differential_diagnoses[2]: Ocular hypertension,Primary optic atrophy (pallor but no cupping of the disc)
complications[3]: Central Retinal Vein Occlusion,Rubeosis irides with resultant secondary glaucoma,Total blindness
prevention[2]: Early detection and prompt treatment,Screening for glaucoma should be incorporated into the health plan of any nation
other_investigations: null
definitive_treatment[6]: Goniotomy (for congenital glaucoma),Trabeculectomy (for all forms of glaucoma),Trabeculotomy,Laser trabeculoplasty,Peripheral iridectomy or Yag laser iridotomy for acute closed angle glaucoma (to the affected eye as well as the normal fellow eye),Laser photo-ablation of the ciliary body
prognosis: null